{
  "case_id": "2008-07-526",
  "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 1:00 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "THEODORE B. OLSON, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioners.\nDEANNE E. MAYNARD, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. OLSON: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nCongress squarely addressed and unambiguously answered the first question in this case when it enacted the Indian Reorganization Act of 1934.\nIt authorized the Secretary to take land in trust for Indians, and it declared, as used in this Act, Indians were \"members of any recognized Indian tribe now under Federal jurisdiction.\" The word \"now\" had the same meaning in 1934 as it does every morning in this Court when the Marshal announces that \"The Court is now sitting.\"\nWhen Congress said \"now under Federal jurisdiction,\" it did not mean \"then under Federal jurisdiction,\" but that is what the Government contends.\nIn fact, the word \"then\" is the antonym for \"now.\"\n\"Now\" must be given its ordinary meaning, which the Government concedes on -- in its brief, is the date,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What about a poster that says \"Give blood now.\"\nMR. OLSON: Pardon me, Justice Breyer? I didn't hear you.\nJUSTICE BREYER: They put up a poster that says \"Give blood now.\"\nMR. OLSON: Well, it is --\nJUSTICE BREYER: It doesn't mean when it was printed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: What sort of -- excuse me.\nWhat sort of tribes were not under Federal jurisdiction?\nMR. OLSON: Well, the use of the word \"tribe\" in that question is -- is causing me a problem momentarily.\nJUSTICE KENNEDY: Pardon me. What -- what -- yes, what members of tribes were not under Federal jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Of course, I suppose if the phrase \"now under the jurisdiction of the United States\" did not have any clear meaning when the statute was enacted, it -- it wouldn't have any clear meaning for the future, either. So you don't -- you don't solve that problem by reading \"now\" to mean \"then,\" right?\nMR. OLSON: Well, what -- what -- I think I understand your question. What the Government wants to do is just take the word \"now\" out of the statute"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Even if they were recognized later?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Olson, let me just make sure I get this off my chest, and then I'll be quiet. The first sentence in section 19 defines the term \"Indian.\" And that's the section you're talking about?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. MAYNARD",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it was a contemporaneous application of the term."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: As you read the statute, Ms. Maynard, the words \"now under Federal jurisdiction\" could be deleted and the statute would mean the same thing that you're urging."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well, there may -- there may not be, but let me on that score, take you back to an answer that Mr. Olson gave."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I wouldn't know that that's so, because the -- the question I ask myself on that is: Were I in Congress, is this the kind of thing I would have delegated to the Secretary to decide."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Can I ask you a question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I'm interested -- I'm interested in the Secretary's conclusion that recognized \"tribe\" and \"tribe now under Federal jurisdiction\" are one and the same; that the words are used redundantly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Secretary can take property from the State, particularly a small State like Rhode Island, but it would be the same anywhere, and strip the State of jurisdiction and give jurisdiction to a dual sovereign operating within that State."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How did it get to be recognized? I thought the recognition reflects that it's had a history going way, way back?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-526",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-890bdffb96a2-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 2:02 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
